# kin/child/legs/tips: the child's shoe tips under a long skirt (robe, kaftan, wrap, gown)
# THE SIDE WALK, KIN-CHILD rollout (2026-10-22): each side walk tip is the two boots of std.pxm + far.pxm's key at the
# same placement, whole (the near over, the far `under`); the long skirt hides their tops, the soles step under the hem.
# Superseded where it differs:
# THE SIDE WALK (the motion rebuild, 2026-10-21, docs/MOTION_P2.md 7.4): each side walk tip is the boot of std.pxm's key
# at the same placement (boots_child.stamps), windowed like the youth's (C0 / C1 whole, C2 its toe end, cols 3-5 R).
# History (superseded for the side walk and run by the rebuild above; front and back keys, the idles and the other
# keys are unchanged):
# kin/child/legs/tips: the child's shoe tips under a long skirt (robe, kaftan, wrap, gown): the boot toes and soles of the
# std legs' F-1 row, stepping with them (a lifted foot hides under the hem). (KIN-CHILD.) Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body child
role legs tips
layer legs
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_child
tags boots-stamped

view R key walkA origin 12 6 stretch 0
put C0n -1 0 cols 0-2
put C0n -1 -1 cols 3-5
put C0f -5 -1 under
